    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just \"building rapport\" though. when i look at the timing of everything, it feels intentional. like, the way i choose to walk a certain route or when i decide to stop and speak to someone... it's like i'm hitting these pressure valves in the social fabric before they explode. like that cafe situation, if i hadn't been there at that exact second, that tension might have spilled over into something much more chaotic for the whole block. i'm starting to wonder if i can actually predict where these friction points are going to appear. how would someone even begin to track these kinds of micro-interventions to make sure they're working?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
